"""Curated data for the numeric scorecard (round 2). Imported by scorecard_extract.py and scorecard.py.

Each ROW is one named physical quantity. Its FACES are the numbers the compendium prints for it
(several faces = several printed readings). For every face, `expr` is the value converted to the
measured quantity named in `ref` (sympy syntax), and `how` says how it was converted from the printed
form. `anchors` are strings that must occur verbatim (whitespace-normalised) in the named statement
unit; scorecard_extract.py checks them.

Field codes
  ident   E  the source states the number as the quantity with a stated normalisation or unit
             (e.g. "under the correspondence the fine-structure constant at zero momentum transfer",
             "in the electron unit")
          N  name / nearest object only ("The correspondence is by name")
          P  the source names only a generic class; the pairing with a measured quantity is ours
  derived R  re-derived here exactly from the construction as stated (scorecard.py, block REDERIVE)
          A  arithmetic from printed inputs checked; the inputs are not derivable from the page
          T  target-like: a cell the source calls a candidate, or a value a rule is fitted to return
          N  stated without derivation on the page
  kind    num (numerical comparison), int (integer / exponent), sign, zero (0 vs nonzero), form
          (functional form or ordering), theory (agreement with a theorem of standard physics, no
          measurement involved), nc (not comparable: dimensionful with no unit map)
  primary index of the face the source adopts ("standing", "adopted", "primary"), or None when it
          prints several faces and selects none.
"""

CODES = {
    "STRUCT": "numerals are counts, registers or dimensions of the construction; no value is given for the named quantity",
    "DUP": "the number is a face already carried by a scorecard row (see note)",
    "NOVAL": "the quantity is named but the unit prints no value for it",
    "MATH": "the named object is mathematical (a group, an algebra, an operator) with no measured value beyond its structure",
    "NOREF": "a number is printed but the named quantity has no measured or textbook counterpart value",
    "AMBIG": "the bodies the number refers to are not identified, so no measured value can be assigned",
    "UNMAPPED": "a dimensionful number in a unit the source leaves unmapped (the tick, the count metric), with no unit-free ratio to a measured quantity",
}

